<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Document</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  body {
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="font-size: 36px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">A Warm Welcome to <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span></h1>
  <p style="font-size: 18px; font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 40px;">-interview by <span data-field="interviewer_name">{{ interviewer_name }}</span> '{{ year }}'</p>

  <div style="display: flex; gap: 40px;">
    <div style="flex: 2;">
      <p style="line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 20px;">This year, the <span data-field="center_name">{{ center_name }}</span> Center was thrilled to welcome <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span>, an accomplished human rights scholar. Born in <span data-field="birth_location">{{ birth_location }}</span>, just as the city-state gained independence, <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span> gained an international perspective on life from a young age. Later, he was admitted to the <span data-field="university_name">{{ university_name }}</span> College of Southeast Asia, which further got him hooked on the wider world and taught him the importance of field research. Since then, he has traveled to over <span data-field="travel_count">{{ travel_count }}</span> countries. His traveling has also enriched his perspective on human rights, and he found himself fascinated by the way one's identity impacts their treatment by governments and organizations. His first publication, titled "<span data-field="publication_title">{{ publication_title }}</span>", examined how the majority of violence victims were men. Through his travels, writings, and photography, <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span> continues to gain prominence and expertise in his field.</p>
      <p style="line-height: 1.6;">Due to their shared expertise in genocide studies, Professor <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span> (Mgrublian Center Director) invited Jones to spend the fall <span data-field="year">{{ year }}</span> semester at CMC as a William F. Podlich Distinguished Fellow. During this time, Jones co-taught with Professor Lower, worked on the fourth edition of <span data-field="book_title">{{ book_title }}</span>, presented his photography through a public art display, and spoke at the <span data-field="venue_name">{{ venue_name }}</span>.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 1;">
      <img src="placeholder_image_1.jpg" alt="Portrait" style="width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 5px;">
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="font-size: 36px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 20px;">A Warm Welcome to <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span></h1>

  <div style="display: flex; gap: 40px;">
    <div style="flex: 1;">
      <img src="placeholder_image_2.jpg" alt="Photo" style="width: 100%; height: auto; margin-bottom: 20px;">
      <img src="placeholder_image_3.jpg" alt="Photo" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 2;">
      <p style="line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 20px;">Jones' <span data-field="event_name">{{ event_name }}</span> talk, "<span data-field="talk_title">{{ talk_title }}</span>", was held early in the fall '{{ year }}' semester and featured his extensive scholarship on genocide and structural violence. In the talk, he proposed analytical angles and empirical standards by which structural violence can be incorporated in a genocide framework, highlighting issue-areas related to Covid-19 that urgently require attention and intervention. The event was well attended by <span data-field="attendee_group">{{ attendee_group }}</span>, staff and faculty and marked a return to in-person Athenaeum dinner events at the college.</p>
      <p style="line-height: 1.6;">In his spare time, <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span> is also an avid photographer, capturing the world through his lens. Through his travels, he focuses his photography on global, historical sites often those which hold painful pasts or were the site of genocidal events.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="font-size: 36px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 20px;">Evoking Genocide Through Photography</h1>

  <div style="display: flex; gap: 40px;">
    <div style="flex: 1;">
      <img src="placeholder_image_4.jpg" alt="Photo" style="width: 100%; height: auto; margin-bottom: 20px;">
      <img src="placeholder_image_5.jpg" alt="Photo" style="width: 100%; height: auto; margin-bottom: 20px;">
      <img src="placeholder_image_6.jpg" alt="Photo" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 2;">
      <p style="line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 20px;">In February, Professor Jones returned to CMC over Parents Weekend to host a photography exhibition titled "<span data-field="exhibition_title">{{ exhibition_title }}</span>". The exhibit featured ten selected photographs and included comments by Jones regarding the challenges of visually evoking the realities and legacies of genocides and mass conflict, both past and present.</p>
      <p style="line-height: 1.6;">Jones' Global Photo Archive comprises <span data-field="photo_count">{{ photo_count }}</span> photos from over <span data-field="country_count">{{ country_count }}</span> countries, including some which were shared during these exhibitions on campus. Posted under a Creative Commons license, these images are used by authors, publishers, academics, students, media outlets, NGOs, and government agencies across the globe and highlight Jones' scholarly work on genocide, war, and human rights. The collection is publicly available and can be found at <span data-field="archive_url">{{ archive_url }}</span>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="font-size: 36px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 20px;">The Middle East: Hot Topics and Challenges in the Region Today</h1>

  <div style="display: flex; gap: 40px;">
    <div style="flex: 1;">
      <p style="line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 20px;">The Mgrublian Center was proud to welcome <span data-field="guest_name">{{ guest_name }}</span> to educate students on the most significant issues faced by the Middle East. <span data-field="guest_name">{{ guest_name }}</span> is a political satirist and foreign policy expert. She worked in the U.S. government for <span data-field="years_of_service">{{ years_of_service }}</span> years in a range of senior national security and public affairs positions. Today, she hosts, writes, and produces her Youtube world news show, "<span data-field="show_name">{{ show_name }}</span>".</p>
      <img src="placeholder_image_7.jpg" alt="Portrait" style="width: 100%; height: auto; margin-top: 20px;">
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 2;">
      <img src="placeholder_image_8.jpg" alt="Panel" style="width: 100%; height: auto; margin-bottom: 20px;">
      <p style="line-height: 1.6;">Drawing from her extensive professional and academic experiences in foreign relations, national security, and public affairs, <span data-field="guest_name">{{ guest_name }}</span> was invited to speak at CMC's Athenaeum. In collaboration with the Mgrublian Center, <span data-field="guest_name">{{ guest_name }}</span> delivered an animated talk during the dinner program and provided insightful commentary on some of the most pressing and ever-evolving topics in the Middle East today.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="font-size: 36px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 20px;">Hitler's Jewish Refugees: Hope and Anxiety in Portugal</h1>

  <div style="display: flex; gap: 40px;">
    <div style="flex: 1;">
      <img src="placeholder_image_9.jpg" alt="Portrait" style="width: 100%; height: auto; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 2;">
      <p style="line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 20px;">On November 9th, the Mgrublian Center hosted a dinner event with <span data-field="speaker_name">{{ speaker_name }}</span>, an esteemed NYU professor of modern Jewish history. At the event, she described the dramatic experiences of Jewish refugees, fleeing Hitler's regime and taking refuge in Portugal. Drawing attention not only to the social and physical upheavals these refugees experienced, <span data-field="speaker_name">{{ speaker_name }}</span> also highlighted the emotional impacts of needing to flee home and beg strangers for kindness. Portugal's dictator at the time, <span data-field="dictator_name">{{ dictator_name }}</span>, admitted the largest number of refugees fleeing westward. However, the dictator set his secret police on those who did not move along quickly enough. To contrast this additional anxiety and violence experienced by the refugees, Portuguese citizens offered shelter, care, and hope to the Jewish population.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="font-size: 36px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 20px;">Movie Screening: Petri Dish, U.S.A.</h1>

  <div style="display: flex; gap: 40px;">
    <div style="flex: 1;">
      <img src="placeholder_image_10.jpg" alt="Movie Poster" style="width: 100%; height: auto; margin-bottom: 20px;">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-around; margin-top: 20px;">
        <img src="placeholder_image_11.jpg" alt="Person" style="width: 30%; height: auto;">
        <img src="placeholder_image_12.jpg" alt="Person" style="width: 30%; height: auto;">
        <img src="placeholder_image_13.jpg" alt="Person" style="width: 30%; height: auto;">
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 2;">
      <p style="line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 20px;">On March 24th, the Center hosted the premier of Matt Leder's (CMC '{{ year }}' documentary film, <span data-field="movie_title">{{ movie_title }}</span>. Leder (pictured at bottom, center), a senior at CMC, was inspired to start this project when he saw the COVID-19 pandemic hit the U.S. prison system especially hard, resulting in a devastating number of inmate fatalities. To begin his work, Leder received a Creative Works Fellowship from the Gould Center to create a documentary that shed light on the deadly consequences manifesting in jails, specifically in the U.S. south. Petri Dish, U.S.A. follows three families as they struggle to secure humane treatment and freedom for their loved ones behind bars. A personal journey as well as a critique of the criminal justice system at large, the film examines our penal system through the lens of the COVID-19 pandemic. What does this virus reveal about our society's relationship with prisons and prisoners, and how might COVID-19 be shaping a new way forward?</p>
      <p style="line-height: 1.6;">In addition to the screening, a Q&A was hosted with two of the film's protagonists: <span data-field="protagonist_1_name">{{ protagonist_1_name }}</span> (bottom left), president of Save Our Sons, and Vicky Scroggins (bottom right), who works with Imprisoned Love Ones Matter.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="font-size: 36px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 20px;">Human Rights Career Panel</h1>

  <div style="display: flex; gap: 40px;">
    <div style="flex: 1;">
